  "question": {
    "text": "A long cylindrical volume contains a uniformly distributed charge of density <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#961;</mi></math>. The radius of cylindrical volume is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi></math>. A charge particle <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi>q</mi></mfenced></math>&nbsp;revolves around the cylinder in a circular path. The kinetic energy of the particle is :"
  },
  "options": [
